{"name":"Sailing","hex":"#869cbb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sailing","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of sail"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Travelling by ship."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sailing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sailing","blocks":[{"text":"Sailing employs the wind—acting on sails, wing sails or kites—to propel a craft on the surface of the water, on ice (iceboat) or on land over a chosen course, which is often part of a larger plan of navigation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Regattafeld_vor_Laboe.jpg/330px-Regattafeld_vor_Laboe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sailing","wikidata":"Q192520"},{"title":"Sailing (sport)","blocks":[{"text":"The sport of sailing involves a variety of competitive sailing formats that are sanctioned through various sailing federations and yacht clubs. Racing disciplines include matches within a fleet of sailing craft, between a pair thereof or among teams. Additionally, there are specialized competitions that include setting speed records. Racing formats include both closed courses and point-to-point contests; they may be in sheltered waters, along coasts, or on the open ocean. Most competitions are held within defined classes or ratings that either entail one type of sailing craft to ensure a contest primarily of skill or rating the sailing craft to create classifications or handicaps."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Mar%C3%ADa_Jos%C3%A9_Poncell_2024.jpg/330px-Mar%C3%ADa_Jos%C3%A9_Poncell_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sailing_(sport)","wikidata":"Q14085739"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Tarangini.jpg/500px-Tarangini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o